<!-- ============ TOOL 1: 3D Mesh Tools ============ -->
<section id="mesh-tools" class="bg-base-200 py-24 border-t-8 border-blue-500">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-14">
      <div class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-400 mb-2">Tool 1</div>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">3D Mesh Tools</h2>
      <p class="text-xl opacity-80">Align and modify STL files from 3D scans. Scans rarely come out clean, watertight or square to anything — fix that in a few clicks, then save an STL that drops straight into CAD, a slicer or a reverse-engineering workflow.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-16">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Level on any face</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80">Pick three points or let it find the largest flat area. Refine the fit by least squares, and flatten a rippled face perfectly flat.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Square, scale &amp; centre</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80">Align an edge to X or Y, scale to a known dimension, and put the origin exactly where you want it — even at the centre of a hole.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Check &amp; repair</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80">One-click health report: holes, loose pieces, non-manifold edges and flipped triangles, labelled on the model. Remove debris and fill small holes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Shrink huge scans</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80">Type the file size you want. A 238&nbsp;MB scan becomes 20&nbsp;MB with the surface moved by thousandths of a millimetre.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Measure</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80">Distances, angles, and the diameter and centre of any hole from three picked points.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Undo &amp; re-use</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80">Every step is undoable and your original is never touched. The 4×4 matrix is saved so you can apply the same move to the full-resolution scan.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-12">
