</section>

<!-- ============ TOOL 2: 3D Mesh Compare ============ -->
<section id="mesh-compare" class="bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-900 to-slate-800 text-white py-24 border-t-8 border-purple-500">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center mb-16">
      <div>
        <div class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-purple-400 mb-2">Tool 2</div>
        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">3D Mesh Compare</h2>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 mb-6">How close is your reverse-engineered model to the scan it came from? Export the model as an STL, line it up with the scan data, and every point is coloured by its distance from the reference surface.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-200 mb-8">
          <li>✓ <strong>Automatic best fit</strong> — tries several starting orientations, so a symmetric part doesn't end up upside down</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Tolerance colour map</strong> — green within tolerance, red for extra material, blue for missing; hover to read the deviation anywhere</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Section view</strong> — cut through the part and see the outline gap, magnified</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Pick a range on the histogram</strong> — everything else turns grey, so problem areas stand out</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Statistics by surface area</strong> — % in tolerance, mean, RMS, 95% band and histogram</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Branded HTML report</strong> — your logo and job details, ready to send to a client (<a class="underline text-purple-300 hover:text-purple-200" href="/demo-report/">see a demo report</a>)</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Batch mode</strong> — run it from the command line for a pile of parts</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <a href="/3dmeshcompare/" class="btn btn-lg bg-purple-600 hover:bg-purple-500 border-0 text-white">3D Mesh Compare guide</a>
          <a href="/demo-report/" class="btn btn-lg btn-outline border-purple-400 text-purple-300 hover:bg-purple-600 hover:text-white">View demo report</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/madjalapeno/3dmeshtools/archive/refs/heads/main.zip" class="btn btn-lg bg-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-600 border-0 text-white">Download</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        {% shot "09-compare-deviation.png", "Deviation colour map, statistics and histogram in 3D Mesh Compare", "Deviation map with statistics and histogram." %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 pt-12 border-t border-slate-700">
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="text-5xl font-bold text-purple-400 mb-3">1</div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Load both</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-300">Open the reference (your model as an STL) and the scan — or drop both files on the window.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="text-5xl font-bold text-purple-400 mb-3">2</div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Align</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-300">One click for automatic best fit, or pick three matching point pairs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="text-5xl font-bold text-purple-400 mb-3">3</div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Inspect &amp; report</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-300">Read the deviation map, pin callouts, and export the HTML report or a CSV.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

